---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { getRelease, repository } from "../lib/release";
const r = await getRelease();
---

<Layout
  title="VeyDock Changelog | Releases and Verification"
  description="The current VeyDock public release and newer development work, kept separate with links to GitHub release notes and verification."
>
  <article class="page wrap">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="eyebrow">RELEASE RECORD / NO INVENTED MILESTONES</p>
      <h1>The work, in public.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Release notes describe the shipped build. Development previews describe
        what is being worked on.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>{r.version} / current public release</h2>
      <p class="mono">
        {new Date(r.date).toLocaleDateString("en-GB")} /{" "}
        {r.prerelease ? "PRERELEASE" : "STABLE"}
      </p>
      <p>
        The actual published installer and release notes are available on
        GitHub. The historical package filename remains visible on the download
        page.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={r.release}>Read the official release notes ↗</a>
      </p>
      <h2>Development interface / not a new release</h2>
      <p>
        The website captures the newer profile-card interface using clearly
        labelled sample data. This is not an announcement of a new desktop
        version. Taskbar icon, layout and sidebar work can be inspected in the
        source history.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={`${repository}/commits/main/`}>Inspect the commit history</a> ·{" "}
        <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md`}>
          Full source changelog
        </a>
      </p>
      <h2>Verification remains visible</h2>
      <p>
        Usage refresh observations, fixture tests and real-desktop acceptance
        are separate kinds of evidence. Consult the{" "}
        <a href={`${repository}/blob/main/VERIFICATION.md`}>
          verification record
        </a>{" "}
        for current status. A website deployment does not complete an
        account-switch test.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
